{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview","id":989672,"title":"Dissapointed by the Netjer preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-18T19:38:17-07:00","id":989672,"title":"Dissapointed by the Netjer preview","content":"I want to preface this by saying both that I mean no offense with any of this post, and that I'm a casual student of Egyptian myth with very little academic backing for my studies. The Netjer have been my favorite pantheon for pretty much my entire life, and I'm a fan of them and of Scion above everything else.<br /> <br /> That said, I am profoundly let down by the Netjer preview we've seen, and have enough individual complaints with it that I'm honestly considering doing a complete rewrite of the Pantheon myself, because I'm not sure the section can be salvaged properly before going to print. I don't want any of this to read as a personal attack on the section's author or their credibility, but at the same time it hurts pretty bad to see so many questionable decisions in my favorite mythology.<br /> <br /> In no particular order (and using Greek names as the text does):<ul><li>I can't think of any reason for Hathor to have not made the list, as one of the eldest (many believe her to predate Egypt as a civilization) and most important gods of the Netjer. She's the patron of women and mothers, a goddess of love and femininity with widespread worship across the breadth and historical length of Egypt. I'd sooner see her cut entirely than merged with Isis, a combination I'm not familiar with having ever happened historically and roughly akin to merging Aphrodite with Hera just because both are goddesses who love; if any merger were to happen it would be with Sekhmet, her fellow solar deity and shared holder of the Eye of Ra title. There's an element of personal bias here (Hathor is my favorite of the Netjer), but at the same time as a student of myth I really can't see any reason for this cut/merger to exist, and citing wordcount really just rings hollow to me.</li> <li>The Pantheon as a whole feels rather grossly mischaracterized; they should relatively grim and stoic, focused on upholding the just and proper way of ma'at (to the point where the Eye of Ra is sent to punish mankind, and souls are condemned to oblivion or the lake of fire for living lives not in accordance with the proper way of things, nevermind how callous that is), yet these Netjer seem a lively, fun bunch who squabble over &quot;family drama&quot; and scarcely paying too much mind to duty. The Virtues attest to a proper treatment of the Netjer as a very traditional bunch who care as much as about doing things the way they've been done for thousands of years according to tradition as they do about doing the right thing, as Ma'at dictates that the latter is strictly the former and nothing else.</li> <li>Why are the Netjer constantly fighting their Titans? Geb and Nut are well-liked, Aten is apparently now another name for Re, and argument could be made for Ma'at as a Titan of Order. I believe Neall had previously said that the Netjer got along quite well with them, too.</li> <li>Each god's write-up is more focused on telling one of their myths than actually saying anything about who they are or what they were the gods of.</li> <li>Nothing in the section describes that the Netjer have sacred animals or that they appear as animals or animal-headed humans. While this is fairly common knowledge, it should come up.</li> <li>They text as a whole is pretty dry and feels very rough. I know this is a first draft, but the Theoi and Tuatha sections were just more pleasant to read overall.</li> <li>Anubis has no reason to be characterized as passionate. His entire purpose in myth is to be the unflinching judge of the dead willing to feed hearts to Ammut and damn souls to oblivion because it is his duty, and it's honestly bizarre to take any reading of Anubis' character in myth as one where he's a caring, emotional sort. He's prepares and judges the dead, so having him out there and fretting over the living just seems absurd. &quot;Anubis never cared if he was the one to read the scales&quot; is a very, very strange reading of a god who existed to do just that.</li> <li>Bast was a guardian above all else, the holy protector of house, home, and Egypt whose sacred animal was possibly the most-loved in the entire culture; writing her off as an insane drunk who randomly beats anyone who dares speak to her seems as incorrect as it does offensive. The Sekhmet merger doesn't make a ton of sense, but if it must happen then it should be reflected as a duality between savagery and civility, the blood-crazed killer who nearly exterminated humanity and the beloved figure whose messengers were more loved than the humans of the empire. She really should have the Guardian Calling, as that was her chief purpose to the Egyptians as both the protector of home and grain and as a defender of the solar boat. Sekhmet was a goddess of medicine as well, so possibly consider giving this weird Bast-Sekhmet the Health Purview.</li> <li>Set and Horus never split Egypt, and suggesting so only makes any sense if we're deliberately trying to subvert the unification of Egypt, which I can't think of any reason to. Horus is king of Egypt proper, and Set rules the 'red lands' of the desert along with the foreign lands beyond.</li> <li>Everything about Isis. Characterizing the noble wife of Osiris as a one who would deal with Apep and try to steal power from Re makes her out to be a thousand time worse than Set is ever depicted at his worst, and she seems like a controlling jerk who aims to control her husband utterly rather than as his loving spouse. Nothing is said of her primarily mythological role as goddess of magic and master of true names, beyond the latter being touched on in her conniving theft of Re's. If she's going to be merged with Hathor (which I am massively opposed to), then her description should focus more on her role as patron of women and embodiment of love and the caring wife, or else drop Hathor as an alternate name for her entirely. Isis has no ties to cows that I'm aware of other than this unfortunate merger with Hathor, so if you must merge them at least mention Hathor as, say, a Mantle with a bovine aspect.</li> <li>Ma'at's description should probably touch on what ma'at meant to the Egyptians: everything in its proper place, everyone performing their appointed duties from birth until death. It was about justice and order, but it was also a force for imposing and protecting a strict hierarchy, and rebelling against a 5000 year-old traditional way that Things Absolutely Have To Be is exactly the kind of thing for scrappy Scions to do in play. I'd honestly make her an allied Titan of Order instead of a god.</li> <li>Osiris is a noble king of the dead, and also the beloved giver of the harvest (you see a lot of art where the harvest sprouts from his corpse); portraying him as a scheming jerk who extorts the dead is against every depiction of him I'm familiar with. There are no Orpheus-style bargains to return from the dead in Egyptian myth <i>as Osiris himself embodies</i>; though returned to life, he still must remain in Duat, as he has died and it is the proper place for the dead. Again I must object to Isis being shown as a petty figure holding his leash who &quot;despises&quot; him, and again I must strongly object to showing Anubis as eager to reject his duty or why the weighing of the heart should be Osiris' task. Also, shouldn't the lord of the dead have the Liminal Calling? And why does the Relationships section make him out to dislike Re?</li> <li>You may want to define the ib as the heart, or else just call it the heart.</li> <li>I'm not sure you want to suggest Aten as an alternate name for Re given that he was a Titan in 1e, and I would at least mention somewhere in the text that Khepri is his aspect as the scarab beetle pushing the sun; it's too iconic a Netjer image to miss.</li> <li>Set is absolutely savaged and painted as an outright evil figure, which I cannot forgive. I don't think I've ever seen a version of the myth where he kills Osiris at Re's command (it's almost always motivated by envy for the throne of Egypt), and if that strange version of myth is the one you want to tell then why is he hated by the Pantheon as a traitor if he was following orders from their highest authority - and aided in it by Thoth?! You can't completely recontextualize the most well-known Egyptian myth and then move on without touching on that. Something definitely should be mentioned regarding his role as the most commonly-depicted guardian of the solar barge and his eternity-long fight with Apep, and it seems odd to have the Egyptian god of foreigners only interact with one foreign god - and adversarially at that! His mortal form should have red hair. Giving him Beasts (Donkey, Pig) is absurd and based wholly in attempts on guessing what the sha beast is, and looks very odd when you go on and describe the sha beast in the Borthrights section. As protector of the travelers, surely he deserves the Journeys Purview, and as the one who walks the boundaries of Egypt and the red lands beyond he's as Liminal as they come.</li> <li>If Nu is going to be the Netjer Overworld (which it shouldn't, as Nu is a member of the Ogdoad and makes much more sense as a Titan of Water) then it should be the primordial sea that predates time and that the universe sprang from. I'm not sure where the inverted earth thing comes from, but Nu has always been a great ocean as well as the god of it. Shouldn't Aaru be their Overworld instead - or more accurately, shouldn't they just have an Underworld?</li> <li>Duat is absolutely full of demons and other perilous threats, to the point where most of all recorded Egyptian religion recorded is advice on how to safely cross through it and protect yourself from its threats. Duat is a dangerous land of magic and monsters with flaming seas and constant challenges for the dead. The text should reflect any of this.</li> <li>Again, if you're going to describe Kemeticism, probably go further into detail on what ma'at actually meant and how it's about performing your duty to civilization and not upsetting the applecart too much. I'd also explore some sample cults for some gods (I'd do one for Bast and one for Thoth, personally), as the Theoi got example Mysteries.</li> <li>Deception has no place as an Asset Skill for the Netjer, as should be readily apparent if you're starting the section with the 42 Confessions. Speaking falsely was a sin worthy of having your soul utterly destroyed in Ammut's jaws, and it's fucking ridiculous to have the Netjer praise that. Occult fits much better, as does whatever Storypath's Empathy-equivalent is.</li> <li>The Relationships section is strange. If the Theoi section is going to mention that the Netjer protected them in the past and currently lord that over them, maybe that should be mentioned. I would definitely explore the idea of West as sacred to the Egyptians and what the Netjer think of the American deities in that context (especially given theories of Egyptian contact with the Americas). I think the dedicated servants of ma'at would get along swimmingly with the proper, orderly Shen, and I think mention should be made of how the Netjer view their immediate Mesopotamian neighbors (and I get that they aren't in this book, but the Tuatha preview touched on the Welsh and Gallic Pantheons).</li> <li>Heku just refers to magic, and makes for a strange PSP given that it... doesn't really describe anything, or rather describes anything magical. I think it could use a more specific name. The sum of everything in the soul is the Sahu, not the Ha. I've never heard Heku used to describe vital life force.</li> </ul>I expected concessions to be made to fun and for some myth to be played with pretty loosely, but this goes well beyond that into being wrong and sometimes offensive. I hope the other Pantheons are treated with more respect, because this is shockingly not-right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-19-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:12:48-07:00","id":989683,"title":"","content":"Well the Overworld shouldn't be Aaru, because Aaru is a paradise for the dead, not the realm of the celestial gods. What I'm thinking for my own table is that the Underworld in general is shadowly lifeless place, but realms tied to specific deities who bridge life and death can become verdant paradises. So Osiris as a resurrecting god of the dead creates Aaru as a paradise sanctum beyond the rest of the Duat, just as Persephone's cycles between the World and the Underworld allow the Elysian Fields to bloom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:14:53-07:00","id":989685,"title":"","content":"Honestly, a lot of the issues that you raise also struck me,--<br /> <br /> --I pretty much assumed, &quot;Huh, I guess I know a lot less about Egyptian Mythology than I thought.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which, you know, didn't hugely surprise me because I have absolutely no scholarly background. I thought I understood these Gods better than this,-- I've generally got a pretty good understanding of the Theoi, for instance, and while there's a few little nitpicks that I'd have with that write-up... nothing really struck me out of the blue or really surprised me..<br /> <br /> (n' I just don't know enough about the other Pantheons at any but the most shallow level to know one way or the other...)<br /> <br /> Like you, I'd rather not have Divinities merged together without very good reason, if only because if they're not merged then one can assume that they were only left out for space and easily toss them into the Pantheon without worry. Like, no Hebe in the Greek! That's fine; I can put here there if I want.<br /> <br /> I like the telling of myths related to the Gods, in general, though I agree that more space could be devoted to explaining about the God in question...<br /> <br /> ...anyway, just my two cents, chiming in supporting the points you made with my own thoughts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:17:59-07:00","id":989688,"title":"","content":"I've suggested the idea that Sutekh killed Azar in part out of LOYALTY to Re, but not at Re's behest - on the notion that Aset stealing Re's Ren came first. But I'd agree him doing at Re's behest would need a lot more fleshing out if they're going with that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:19:11-07:00","id":989689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989685#post989685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, a lot of the issues that you raise also struck me,--<br /> <br /> --I pretty much assumed, &amp;quot;Huh, I guess I know a lot less about Egyptian Mythology than I thought.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Which, you know, didn't hugely surprise me because I have absolutely no scholarly background. I thought I understood these Gods better than this,-- I've generally got a pretty good understanding of the Theoi, for instance, and while there's a few little nitpicks that I'd have with that write-up... nothing really struck me out of the blue or really surprised me..<br /> <br /> (n' I just don't know enough about the other Pantheons at any but the most shallow level to know one way or the other...)<br /> <br /> Like you, I'd rather not have Divinities merged together without very good reason, if only because if they're not merged then one can assume that they were only left out for space and easily toss them into the Pantheon without worry. Like, no Hebe in the Greek! That's fine; I can put here there if I want.<br /> <br /> I like the telling of myths related to the Gods, in general, though I agree that more space could be devoted to explaining about the God in question...<br /> <br /> ...anyway, just my two cents, chiming in supporting the points you made with my own thoughts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be less mad about the mergers if it wasn't handled as &quot;and this god also goes by another name and nevermind the fact that that second name has an entirely different personality and associations.&quot; If the Bast section said that Sekhmet came to earth to slay mankind and was tamed with copious offerings of beer that turned her from a fierce lioness into a gentle housecat, that would be one thing, but this doesn't even bother with that.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;Isis, also known as Hathor&quot; and then only talking about Isis myths while stapling a Cows Purview to her is not a fair treatment of Hathor, and I'd sooner see her not mentioned at all than whatever the hell this is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:30:56-07:00","id":989692,"title":"","content":"Yeah, rather disappointed with this. I'll probably have to completely remake them if I end up playing Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:33:44-07:00","id":989693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989692#post989692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, rather disappointed with this. I'll probably have to completely remake them if I end up playing Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go ahead and rewrite them myself if the writers don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:35:50-07:00","id":989694,"title":"","content":"I gotta say? I think I agree with you about most of this.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe merger of Isis and Hathor makes no damn sense. They are two very distinct and separate goddesses who both deserve their own write-up.<br /> <br /> \u200bIsis can be conniving, but this write-up makes her sound flat-out evil and cruel. I don't agree with that at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bSet is a mix of good and evil. He does bad things, but he's also Ra's most stalwart defender. It makes no sense to portray him this way.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's almost like the writer is trying to get the Netjer to &quot;out-Theoi the Theoi,&quot; or something. I'm worried about this, and I hope that this thread will be considered a good sounding board for fan concerns for the devs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T20:36:10-07:00","id":989695,"title":"","content":"The core 12 I'm inclined to go with at my table (with Ma'at as a distant but honored primordial figure rather than a ruler)<br /> <br /> Re (with his primary Mantles being Khepri for the dawn, Atum-Re the Creator for noonday sun, Khnum the shaper for dusk, and the unseen Amun-Re at night)<br /> <br /> Azar<br /> <br /> Aset (she is not petty, she is however Machievellian, and is the political shadow behind the thrones of Re, Azar, and Heru simultaneously)<br /> <br /> Sutekh<br /> <br /> Nephthys (she's so loosely defined, I can go with the Purview set they were using for Ma'at, and just replace Ostrich with Kite)<br /> <br /> Heru<br /> <br /> Hathor/Sekhmet (two mantles of the same goddess, one a creator/fertility goddess, the other a destroyer/war goddess; wife of Heru)<br /> <br /> Djheuty<br /> <br /> Bastet (At one point simply another name of Sekhmet, but this Mantle grew into a separate being that may be a Scion who seized a spare name; while lioness Sekhmet is a fierce direct warrior as Eye of Re, the cat Bast is a guardian and assassin in darkness where he is unseen)<br /> <br /> Sebek<br /> <br /> Anpu<br /> <br /> Ptah<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (I like the idea of the infinite forms of the Ogdoad themselves [who can be Primordials instead of Titans] being the Overworld of the Netjer, but that should be explicitly the case rather than just using Nu as a catchall term)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:52:45-07:00","id":989717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview#post989672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, shouldn't the lord of the dead have the Liminal Calling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can't speak for a LOT of the writeup, what with my understanding of the Netjer coming from Age of Mythology and finding Gods of Egypt to be rather pretty brain junk food, but gonna throw in my... Haypenny, it's not even two cents worth.<br /> <br /> But the Liminal, while Psychopomps and Lords of Death DO have it, doesn't <i>universally </i>apply to Gods of the Underworld. It's for those who travel, those who guide, those who straddle multiple worlds. IIRC, Hermes has the Liminal Calling.<br /> <br /> Osiris, by your own admission, is <i>trapped</i> in the Underworld. As in cannot cross between the worlds.<br /> <br /> So he cannot be a Liminal. Anubis is more of a Liminal, being one who guides the dead to their final resting place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:56:51-07:00","id":989719,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading this preview, and I must say that it needs some serious work. It's starting to look like gods (that is to say goddesses, you'll note none of the dudes are being forces to share a bunk) are only being merged for the sake of page/word count, and that kind of sloppiness honestly makes me want to withdraw my pledge.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised, given the attention the Kickstarter has garnered, that things aren't expanding to the point where we get Pantheon books for each of the major pantheons. Something a bit more general in the core books would be sufficient, and those of us who care about a particular pantheon over the others can then buy the Pantheon book for them, you could even make said releases PDF only to avoid printing costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:01:02-07:00","id":989720,"title":"","content":"Oh, I SO agree with the objections to this, to the point where it would have seriously undermined my enthusiasm for the game if this had been the first Pantheon previewed. For all of Lex's reasons, the general tone, and the overall seeming lack of respect and understanding of the Egyptian deities, I sincerely hope this gets an overhaul before final draft. Add Nephthys, split Hathor, Isis, Bast and Sekhmet - who cares if some myths say they could be unified? One period of history replaced all the Netjer with Amun, and we aren'the using that version, are we? More potential patrons isn'the a bad thing. Are you going to unite Kali, Durgha, Lakshmi, Parvati, and Sarasvati because they are all part of the same female principal of Hinduism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:01:35-07:00","id":989721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989719#post989719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[A]nd that kind of sloppiness honestly makes me want to withdraw my pledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's be fair. Three Pantheons have been previewed, out of the ten that'll be in the core, and the 2.5 that'll be in the Companion.<br /> <br /> Of those, the Theoi and the Tuatha sections were good. Great, even.<br /> <br /> The Netjer one may not live up to the other two, but is missing one out of three really enough to make you consider withdrawing your pledge from what is otherwise a really promising project?<br /> <br /> Were the Netjer your make or break for the game? Do you not care about the other Pantheons?<br /> <br /> Honestly, given the track record so far, I'd say a more reasonable response would be &quot;I'm disappointed, because I know this game can do better&quot; and maybe <i>seeing what the rounds of editing do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:13:54-07:00","id":989722,"title":"","content":"But if it's your favorite Pantheon, then it's really disappointing when they aren't treated with respect. And if this one is so bad, who's to say that the others won't be the same? Yes, the Theoi and Tuatha were great - but the Netjer is really bad, so that's 33% of the previewed Pantheons so far that are a disappointment. Hopefully, the devs will read this, and make some hasty changes, so the Netjer can be as great as the other two we've seen. And they will treat the other 11 Pantheons we have coming with a bit more TLC - after all, the game is all about the Gods and their Scions, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:16:53-07:00","id":989724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989721#post989721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, let's be fair. Three Pantheons have been previewed, out of the ten that'll be in the core, and the 2.5 that'll be in the Companion.<br /> <br /> Of those, the Theoi and the Tuatha sections were good. Great, even.<br /> <br /> The Netjer one may not live up to the other two, but is missing one out of three really enough to make you consider withdrawing your pledge from what is otherwise a really promising project?<br /> <br /> Were the Netjer your make or break for the game? Do you not care about the other Pantheons?<br /> <br /> Honestly, given the track record so far, I'd say a more reasonable response would be &quot;I'm disappointed, because I know this game can do better&quot; and maybe <i>seeing what the rounds of editing do</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were fine, I wouldn't say they were 'great', that's just a matter of personal opinion on my part. I personally had no interest in the Tuatha pantheon, and the preview for that didn't really change my feelings.<br /> <br /> I've already decided that without some substantial changes I'm completely rewriting the Netjer pantheon. If the Aztec pantheon is anything like it was in the first edition book, that's also getting rewritten for the sake of my players, as I have a very different take on them that closely ties them to the Mayan and Olmec pantheons, which I will also have to create myself as they aren't part of the official release.<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm really almost using the books purely for their mechanics, and not their actual fluff. You could argue that threatening to drop a pledge over one pantheon is overreacting, but for me I've already been considering whether or not investing in both books in hard copy is worth it, and things like this give solid pushes toward either canceling my pledge entirely, or dropping it down to the significantly cheaper PDF pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:20:19-07:00","id":989726,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, I'm not saying that you should accept the pantheon if you feel there's very serious problems with it. I'm more objecting to &quot;The first draft that's due for revision isn't up to what I hoped. I'm taking my donation and leaving&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, Neall and the team have earned a level of trust, IMO, with their openness and willingness to talk to the fans, and post these previews. And in exchange, I think it's more than fair to at least wait for them to say &quot;We've taken the response into account and will be addressing it in the revision process&quot; before saying &quot;Well I'm considering withdrawing my donation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because they've at least earned a chance to say their piece, and the first two previews being great, along with the very visible passion the writer for the Manitou put in his posts, makes me think that there's very real passion and a wish to do justice to the Pantheons here.<br /> <br /> They made a mistake, apparently. Give them a chance to fix it before getting all doom and gloom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:24:34-07:00","id":989729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989719#post989719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (that is to say goddesses, you'll note none of the dudes are being forces to share a bunk)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. Look at all the conflations on Re for crying out loud! The ascent and descent of rival cults in Egyptian history resulted in the constant synchronizing and separating of deities. I don't agree with conflating Hathor and Aset either, but it's not like it's a thing the writers made up that never happened in Ancient Egyptian religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:25:15-07:00","id":989730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989726#post989726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more objecting to &quot;The first draft that's due for revision isn't up to what I hoped. I'm taking my donation and leaving&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Did someone say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:26:41-07:00","id":989732,"title":"","content":"I guess I see it this way; the whole point is, this game is being supported by the real Scion fans at this point [and there are a lot of us, it seems!], and most of us are very much into mythology. Therefore, it also seems logical that the Pantheons should be acceptable [not perfect, since there is no such thing] to those of us who appreciate them. Nothing can ever hit ALL the notes, and no-one expects them to, but the Netjer as presented just don't work, and I for one don't want to have to house-rule entire Pantheons just to play them. That smacks a little too much of 1st edition for me. And if someone doesn't like what they see, then pulling their money in protest is a pretty serious way to make that point. I haven't gone that far, but I hope I'm not as disappointed with the final product as I am with this.<br /> Edit: I certainly will give them a chance to fix this - that's why we're complaining and commenting in the first place! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:30:30-07:00","id":989733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989730#post989730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did someone say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you got me, they only said &quot;That kind of sloppiness honestly makes me want to withdraw my pledge&quot;, probably engaging in a bit of exaggeration to make a point.<br /> <br /> Which I could understand if one of the authors popped in and said &quot;To those with problems with the Nejter writeup: Tough titties, it's our game&quot;.<br /> <br /> They haven't done that yet. They haven't said anything yet. All I'm really trying to say is &quot;Before we make any conclusions about the rest of the game, let's at least wait before saying 'abandon ship'.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989732#post989732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I certainly will give them a chance to fix this - that's why we're complaining and commenting in the first place! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And unlike, say, the Ex3 kickstarter, I imagine this will have actual positive results. Rather than previews of Exalted being met with such nitpicking critique that the Devs basically stopped giving previews.<br /> <br /> (Good GOD the Ex3 Kickstarter was a mess)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-19-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:33:22-07:00","id":989734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989726#post989726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, I'm not saying that you should accept the pantheon if you feel there's very serious problems with it. I'm more objecting to &amp;quot;The first draft that's due for revision isn't up to what I hoped. I'm taking my donation and leaving&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Like, Neall and the team have earned a level of trust, IMO, with their openness and willingness to talk to the fans, and post these previews. And in exchange, I think it's more than fair to at least wait for them to say &amp;quot;We've taken the response into account and will be addressing it in the revision process&amp;quot; before saying &amp;quot;Well I'm considering withdrawing my donation&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Because they've at least earned a chance to say their piece, and the first two previews being great, along with the very visible passion the writer for the Manitou put in his posts, makes me think that there's very real passion and a wish to do justice to the Pantheons here.<br /> <br /> They made a mistake, apparently. Give them a chance to fix it before getting all doom and gloom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm here because I care about mythology and especially because I love the Netjer, and I've just been shown that the person in charge of their section has fundamentally mishandled nearly every aspect of them. Do I trust that this will be fixed and wave my money goodbye with the very real possibility on the table that no substantial revisions will be done and I'm paying for books that misrepresent the very reason I'm here in the first place, or do I vote with my wallet and not support a project that, in the one regard I have any personal knowledge of, has fumbled things pretty significantly?<br /> <br /> I trust Neall, and I think Scion 2e is a fantastic game from everything we've seen. But the Netjer matter to me, seeing them mishandled so drastically hurts pretty deeply, and the only influence I have over the project is my pledge, which I have less than three days to make up my mind with, and I doubt we'll get a revised draft withon three days if we do at all. The option I'd be happiest with is a total redo, and since that's unlikely to happen, I have to make a decision with my money here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-19-2016, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:34:07-07:00","id":989735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989729#post989729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they are. Look at all the conflations on Re for crying out loud! The ascent and descent of rival cults in Egyptian history resulted in the constant synchronizing and separating of deities. I don't agree with conflating Hathor and Aset either, but it's not like it's a thing the writers made up that never happened in Ancient Egyptian religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine with him, because he actually is conflated, all the time, in the mythology. The conflations done with the goddesses, as pointed out, are incredibly off the mark. It's apparent that they are done to save space, and by the same logic you could argue that gods like Anubis and Osiris are actually the same, and Osiris only pretends to be Anubis in order to leave the underworld.<br /> <br /> Except in practice the logic isn't working both ways. I'm not going to turn an off hand comment into a damned crusade, it's an observation, but is an observation that troubles me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989726#post989726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, I'm not saying that you should accept the pantheon if you feel there's very serious problems with it. I'm more objecting to &quot;The first draft that's due for revision isn't up to what I hoped. I'm taking my donation and leaving&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be fine, if I didn't disagree with absolutely everything in the preview, it's not an issue of a concept that is in need of some revisions, it's an issue of disagreeing with the fundamental direction the pantheon has taken in their source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:36:01-07:00","id":989736,"title":"","content":"Also, I've protested the Hathor/Isis merger as utterly nonsensical for the two months since Neall announced it and never got any feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:51:56-07:00","id":989741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview#post989672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Deception has no place as an Asset Skill for the Netjer, as should be readily apparent if you're starting the section with the 42 Confessions. Speaking falsely was a sin worthy of having your soul utterly destroyed in Ammut's jaws, and it's fucking ridiculous to have the Netjer praise that. Occult fits much better, as does whatever Storypath's Empathy-equivalent is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to double-plus on this.<br /> <br /> Think about it for a minute - Egypt has been <i>the</i> byword for magic throughout civilization, rivaled only dimly by Babylon and Persia. Daily magical ritual was a constant practice of the Egyptian household. They have not one, not two, but <i>three or more</i> gods explicitly devoted to magic (Thoth, Seshat, Isis - and that's not even counting the personified god of magic itself, Heka, or their companions Hu (magical utterance) and Sia (magical knowledge)).<br /> <br /> Deception having any part of the Egyptian gods is doubly absurd. Maybe if someone's daddy is Set, sure, but barring that, I really don't think there's an excuse here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T23:10:33-07:00","id":989743,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a>: I think this thread could use you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T23:54:33-07:00","id":989748,"title":"","content":"Why can't I view the preview? Is the link dead or did they take it down or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:00:20-07:00","id":989751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989748#post989748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't I view the preview? Is the link dead or did they take it down or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try this link: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kcG5hU2hWX1JrMVE/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01...hWX1JrMVE/view</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:05:53-07:00","id":989752,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> Although now that I've actually read the OP I'm less inclined to read it. I was willing to give the Isis/Hathor thing a pass out of the various concessions a modern myth roleplaying game requires, but we'll see. My Egyptian mythological knowledge consists of Age of Mythology, Mummy the Curse (which I <i>know</i> made concessions not just for a game but with the intent of presenting an alternate interpretation), and what I've forgotten from school &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:10:26-07:00","id":989753,"title":"","content":"Let me be the first to say that before I came into this thread, I knew next to nothing about Egyptian myth. Every thing I knew was from rough summaries of the myths and Rick Riordan's Kane Chronicles series. And as divisive as Rick Riordan's works can be on here, can I argue that he handled Egyptian mythology better than this preview? <br /> <br /> Please, any member of the Scion team reading this: a significant portion of your fan base is unhappy with this pantheon. Like, bad enough that some people are considering canceling their pledges. Please, please, listen to what we have to say and the sooner you respond to our concerns, the faster you can restore our faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:10:44-07:00","id":989754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989752#post989752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.<br /> <br /> Although now that I've actually read the OP I'm less inclined to read it. I was willing to give the Isis/Hathor thing a pass out of the various concessions a modern myth roleplaying game requires, but we'll see. My Egyptian mythological knowledge consists of Age of Mythology, Mummy the Curse (which I <i>know</i> made concessions not just for a game but with the intent of presenting an alternate interpretation), and what I've forgotten from school &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy gets away with it because it deliberately says &quot;this isn't Egypt, this is fucked-up alien necromancer pre-Egypt&quot; and also is deliberately trying to subvert things, like with Sutekh being the secret good guy, all the sacred animals being mixed around, and the 42 Assessors becoming massively important instead of just a footnote. That level of messing with things requires an understanding of the mythology being messed with, which CAS, Stolze, and everyone else seem to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:34:48-07:00","id":989762,"title":"","content":"I love Eygptian myth and while I am trying to be optimistic, the truth is that that I can't understand what made them choose this direction. It's one thing to give in to and encourage modern myths that may not be accurate in the past, it's another to re-interpret myth to such a degree it is only recognizable in the names and general events, wholly forsaking themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:01:19-07:00","id":989767,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> I admit, the time limit hadn't occurred to me. But given the degree of this negative reaction (which I would like to stress I am not saying you're not allowed to have, so many people disagreeing with this interpretation makes me inclined to accept that maybe they need another pass) I've no doubt that someone will address it soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:27:28-07:00","id":989788,"title":"","content":"This will definitely not be addressed in three days. It cannot and it should not be. Another draft of the Netjer will require time and thought being put into it.<br /> <br /> also, I think Neall has answered the question of the Hathor/Aset thing like, multiple times?<br /> <br /> But, it's worth noting that this draft feels... Dissimilar to what Neall was discussing the conception of the Netjer to be. Miscommunications happen, and this is exactly the sort of thing that having a first draft, 2nd draft and development passes are meant to handle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:28:31-07:00","id":989789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989788#post989788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will definitely not be addressed in three days. It cannot and it should not be. Another draft of the Netjer will require time and thought being put into it.<br /> <br /> also, I think Neall has answered the question of the Hathor/Aset thing like, multiple times?<br /> <br /> But, it's worth noting that this draft feels... Dissimilar to what Neall was discussing the conception of the Netjer to be. Miscommunications happen, and this is exactly the sort of thing that having a first draft, 2nd draft and development passes are meant to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>His answer is &quot;we merged them because of wordcount&quot; which is pretty much a non-answer to me.<br /> <br /> But it is strange to see this draft have nothing to do with everything he's said about the Netjer previously. The whole text feels very rushed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:47:03-07:00","id":989801,"title":"","content":"Well, you've been asking them repeatedly for a Netjer preview. Sometimes you actually don't want to see how the sausage is made. It's usually one of the reasons developers can be cagey with first draft previews.<br /> <br /> I thought couple of times I've seen him answer the question that he's mentioned that they were syncretized at a point and that the choice to merge them in the game reflects that.<br /> <br /> I don't recall him extending that to other combinations, but yeah.<br /> <br /> The disconnect between his description of the Netjer and the concept presented here suggests to me that it's going to be a section that'll make use of the drafting and editing processes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-19-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T04:50:49-07:00","id":989828,"title":"","content":"What i think about every preview is: We have to wait. everything can change of every single detail of the entire game<br /> <br /> just wait and hope everything is going to be great.<br /> <br /> But, nothing is perfect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T05:35:09-07:00","id":989834,"title":"","content":"Hopefully this can be addressed before the kickstarter is over.<br /> <br /> It <i>can</i> be addressed, even if we can't expect to see the final draft before the kickstarter is over.<br /> <br /> Netjer are definitely in my top three favorite pantheons and this is very disappointing. I don't want to reduce my pledge, but I <i>might</i> because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:38:57-07:00","id":989849,"title":"","content":"It's a game not a mytholgy essay/book, the author/s has/have taken some creative license chill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2768-zorker","name":"Zorker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:51:41-07:00","id":989855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989762#post989762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Eygptian myth and while I am trying to be optimistic, the truth is that that I can't understand what made them choose this direction. It's one thing to give in to and encourage modern myths that may not be accurate in the past, it's another to re-interpret myth to such a degree it is only recognizable in the names and general events, wholly forsaking themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this &quot;not accuracy&quot; is actually &quot;they went with a different interpretation than you are used to&quot; - like the it is true that Sekhmet and Bast were originally upper and lower Egyptian names of the same lion headed, drunken goddess of war and prophesy. But under the united kingdom Bast became more distinct.<br /> <br /> Hathor and Aset are conflated in later carvings to the point that without name labels they're often indistinguishable.<br /> <br /> I'm not sayin these are the choices I'd have gone with either, but acting like there's some specific &quot;accurate&quot; version of thousands of years of shifting myth is absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:40:19-07:00","id":989866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989789#post989789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His answer is &amp;quot;we merged them because of wordcount&amp;quot; which is pretty much a non-answer to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give a longer response, but let me clarify one thing - we didn't merge them because of wordcount. I'm sorry I gave that impression. We merged them due to similarity and aspect or because of historical synchretization or trying to look at the gods as singular figures over a period of thousands of years, not because of wordcount. Wordcount is why we chose to put in Ptah instead of Nephthys, for example. Again, sorry about the miscommunication. <br /> <br /> Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:42:13-07:00","id":989868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989855#post989855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sayin these are the choices I'd have gone with either, but acting like there's some specific &amp;quot;accurate&amp;quot; version of thousands of years of shifting myth is absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not dismissing concerns or qualms about the material, but yes, this accurately sums up the issue. The Egyptians suffer from it more than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:53:54-07:00","id":989871,"title":"","content":"And I am in no way trying to step on toes, but maybe this is a case where popular knowledge/perception should take precedence over mythical accuracy? Hathor and Isis are distinct in most well-known myths, as are Bast and Sekhmet (and there has been a chorus asking for Sekhmet since 1st edition), and so I think that's what many of us were expecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:00:02-07:00","id":989875,"title":"","content":"Aaand now I'm bummed Nephthys is missing lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:17:03-07:00","id":989884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989871#post989871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I am in no way trying to step on toes, but maybe this is a case where popular knowledge/perception should take precedence over mythical accuracy? Hathor and Isis are distinct in most well-known myths, as are Bast and Sekhmet (and there has been a chorus asking for Sekhmet since 1st edition), and so I think that's what many of us were expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind hearing new stuff about the myths, honestly, as long as its not just baked up entirely.<br /> <br /> I mean, if there are myths where Isis tried to feed Ra to Apep, I'd definitely like to be told about that,-- that's interesting,-- even if it did completely catch me off-guard.<br /> <br /> This could be a problem of, you know, 'People are generally familiar with the subject material, so the ACTUAL material looks weird,'-- but even so, that's an issue that needs to be addressed, and ideally can be through <i>better writing</i> rather than just writing what we all already know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:22:49-07:00","id":989889,"title":"","content":"What they did there (Aset feeding Re to Apep) is interpreting the story of his deadly viper bite in a way that makes sense as deadly to a god in Scion. Equating that viper with Apep makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:59:02-07:00","id":989929,"title":"","content":"It is due to my own biases, but I admit I was disappointed that Set's description did not mention that he is also the God of Foreigners. I just find that a rather fascinating purview. I think it would be a neat aspect to bring up, even if it would likely not dominate his portrayal. I am curious how that would impact his outlook of the World, and the makeup of his cults, in an increasingly globalized world. Maybe his cult, while not nearly as popular as the Cult of Isis or the other big names ones, is surprisingly wide-spread due to it.<br /> <br /> He was also associated with foreign gods, for good or for ill (often for ill, at least once associated with foreign oppressors), so it could be interesting if the Netjer assume he is one of their prime diplomats. You know those other gods, don't you? Put in a nice word for us. Which the other pantheons might not take as a kind gesture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:08:14-07:00","id":989937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989866#post989866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this is really the best answer I expected considering the situation. Thanks for taking the time to address these concerns, Neall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:11:11-07:00","id":989938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989855#post989855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of this &quot;not accuracy&quot; is actually &quot;they went with a different interpretation than you are used to&quot; - like the it is true that Sekhmet and Bast were originally upper and lower Egyptian names of the same lion headed, drunken goddess of war and prophesy. But under the united kingdom Bast became more distinct.<br /> <br /> Hathor and Aset are conflated in later carvings to the point that without name labels they're often indistinguishable.<br /> <br /> I'm not sayin these are the choices I'd have gone with either, but acting like there's some specific &quot;accurate&quot; version of thousands of years of shifting myth is absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood me.<br /> <br /> I specifically said I don't mind inaccuracy, I have defended Loki having Fire for instance. Even though it is not accurate, it is thematically appropriate and makes use of modern myth. The Netjer write-up does have many accurate tellings, but the way they chose it betrayed the themes of the Netjer. It's one thing to be inaccurate to benefit story and mythological constructs, it's another to choose the version that loses it's themes and sense of story.<br /> <br /> I mean one could write up the Theoi to seem like evil creatures who prey on others with a complete sense of amorality and anyone under their thumb lives a hellish existence. There's enough myth that you stress those cruelties you could easily make an &quot;accurate&quot; Theoi who come off as pure evil. But that's a betrayal of their complexities and stories/themes. This is similiar. The individual myths being played with/conflated don't bother me.<br /> <br /> In fact, I was defending the Merging of the goddesses at one point, I get why and it makes sense with me. I don't really like how it was executed Sekhmet/Bast. But Isis/Hathor I supported far more than Isis being made into a petty goddess hating everyone because she could. Or Anubis abandoning his post. Or Maat being a goddess of deception. 1 or 2 of the elements is okay, but together they just aren't the Netjer anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:18:28-07:00","id":989944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989875#post989875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaand now I'm bummed Nephthys is missing lol</div> </div> </div> </div>so am I- she is my favorite goddess after all. While I understand that she is not there out of wordcount, I don't understand why her very existence seem to have been removed to the point it says that Thoth gave Nut four extra days instead of five. It just don't make sense, especially since it kinda mess with the real egyptian calendar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:23:11-07:00","id":989945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989866#post989866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll give a longer response, but let me clarify one thing - we didn't merge them because of wordcount. I'm sorry I gave that impression. We merged them due to similarity and aspect or because of historical synchretization or trying to look at the gods as singular figures over a period of thousands of years, not because of wordcount. Wordcount is why we chose to put in Ptah instead of Nephthys, for example. Again, sorry about the miscommunication.<br /> <br /> Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A thing I've been wondering about is why the gods would be combined at all at this point in time. Obviously clinging to 'the source material' is a good idea, but it follows that as time goes on a pantheon would spread, not congeal. So for example you could justify the conjunctions of certain gods in old egypt as being politically convenient, or it's the scion of an existing god existing in their parent or sibling's shadow, etc. <br /> <br /> But at this point in time it's fair to say we have access to information to various mythologies that the Egyptians don't have. Many of them, unless they were priests, might not know much about a god that isn't immediately relevant to their city or station, or else they might combine two gods for ease, that reflects on a sprawling empire well enough, but does it reflect on a pantheon of gods, particularly in a game where creating a legend for yourself is one of the main elements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:27:04-07:00","id":989946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989944#post989944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so am I- she is my favorite goddess after all. While I understand that she is not there out of wordcount, I don't understand why her very existence seem to have been removed to the point it says that Thoth gave Nut four extra days instead of five. It just don't make sense, especially since it kinda mess with the real egyptian calendar...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I still think the demand exists for Pantheon books on par with the vampire clanbooks or equivalent. Sadly it's probably way too early to be talking about something like that when the initial kickstarter isn't even complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:32:17-07:00","id":989950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989946#post989946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And I still think the demand exists for Pantheon books on par with the vampire clanbooks or equivalent. Sadly it's probably way too early to be talking about something like that when the initial kickstarter isn't even complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, way too early. But there IS a bit of precedence for what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> 1E had the Scion Ragnarok book, which was mostly focused on the Aesir. Even had an adventure about the Aesir Scion group playing through Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't mind if there were like, smaller booklets concerning &quot;The other little things from the core Pantheons we couldn't fit in the book&quot;, with things like Other Patron Gods, more themed monsters, and other Birthright examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:32:26-07:00","id":989951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989866#post989866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll give a longer response, but let me clarify one thing - we didn't merge them because of wordcount. I'm sorry I gave that impression. We merged them due to similarity and aspect or because of historical synchretization or trying to look at the gods as singular figures over a period of thousands of years, not because of wordcount. Wordcount is why we chose to put in Ptah instead of Nephthys, for example. Again, sorry about the miscommunication. <br /> <br /> Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the prompt response. I hope none of this came off as rude, I just wanted to lay out my greivances at the earliest possible point so they could possibly be fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989945#post989945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A thing I've been wondering about is why the gods would be combined at all at this point in time. Obviously clinging to 'the source material' is a good idea, but it follows that as time goes on a pantheon would spread, not congeal. So for example you could justify the conjunctions of certain gods in old egypt as being politically convenient, or it's the scion of an existing god existing in their parent or sibling's shadow, etc. <br /> <br /> But at this point in time it's fair to say we have access to information to various mythologies that the Egyptians don't have. Many of them, unless they were priests, might not know much about a god that isn't immediately relevant to their city or station, or else they might combine two gods for ease, that reflects on a sprawling empire well enough, but does it reflect on a pantheon of gods, particularly in a game where creating a legend for yourself is one of the main elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it from a gameplay/fun perspective, having the gods be distincy individuals makes morse sense: I'm sure most groups would rather have both a berserker lion goddess of war and wine in addition to a reserved cat mother guardian rather than one divine parent that tries to do both, and having both a goddess of magic and a goddess of women and love allows for many more character concepts than just the former plus a Cows Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:48:48-07:00","id":989960,"title":"","content":"I got to admit I'm being much more upset than I normally would be, I have 2 really painful ear infections and nothing to do but be online all day, so I apologize that I was being overly hostile.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is I wish you'd picked different aspects of the Egyptian gods to stress and actually it would go a long way if I knew why you went the direction you did rather then all the other ones, but I have admitted before and after the preview that Eygpt is really hard to decide on and trying to make sense of it is the process thats never really done. You could make 6 radically different pantheons that are all mythologically accurate and not at all similar to each other from their expanse of history. I get that, everyone has their favorite stories and stresses so matter what it was going to be difficult. It's not something I could have done better, and I am curious how you will change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:03:34-07:00","id":989966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989960#post989960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make 6 radically different pantheons that are all mythologically accurate and not at all similar to each other from their expanse of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Now THAT'S a campaign idea.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright, you're the Scion of Anubis as he was two hundred years before the division between Upper and Lower Egypt... Player 2 is the Scion of Anubis-as-he-was circa 200 years after the division, Lower Egypt flavored... Player 3, you're the Scion of Anubis circa 300 years post-division, Upper Egypt Flavor... And what about you, Player Four?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm the daughter of ALL aspects of Re at once. My Scion has like <i>so many fathers</i>!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... Right.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:51:45-07:00","id":989996,"title":"","content":"As someone who was an anthropology major:<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for us, for the Scion team, and for everyone who likes myth in general... Egyptian myth is a mess, on par with or even more so than Greek/Roman. Most of the stories we know are... Well... Hard to distinguish between. We have a lot of tales BY the Greeks/Romans on Egyptian gods actually. And every tale you know as a casual fan of Egyptian myth has ten more versions known.<br /> <br /> <br /> The truth is: the hard, factual, 'canon' information we have about the Egyptian gods is... Basically enough to fill a single paragraph of description for Ra, and maybe two or three others. Everything else is so incredibly subjective that you could never write a good Egyptian pantheon and not change them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do think that leaving the gods unmerged and just going 'and there's other gods too, who aren't represented here' is the best option though. Just because it means that we might get their write ups one day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:02:09-07:00","id":990003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989875#post989875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaand now I'm bummed Nephthys is missing lol</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can't imagine it being hard to write her up.<br /> <br /> Nephthys<br /> \u200bCallings: Gaurdian, Leader, Liminal<br /> \u200bPurviews: Beasts (Kite), Death, Health, Sun, Journeys","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:03:06-07:00","id":990006,"title":"","content":"I was highly amused by Bast being the god of getting into drunken fist-fights. In any games I run, though, I'm probably going to go with Sekhmet-Hathor and make Bastet the later Greek face applied to it. Make Bastet what happens when Sekhmet-Hathor wanders drunkenly into Greece and accidentally starts a Mystery Cult.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to complain; I found it cute. There was no way one definite story could capture the richness of diverse Egyptian myth in its entirety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:07:54-07:00","id":990010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989951#post989951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Looking at it from a gameplay/fun perspective, having the gods be distincy individuals makes morse sense: I'm sure most groups would rather have both a berserker lion goddess of war and wine in addition to a reserved cat mother guardian rather than one divine parent that tries to do both, and having both a goddess of magic and a goddess of women and love allows for many more character concepts than just the former plus a Cows Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bExcept Mantles seem to do just that, Ares is almost literally 2 different gods in his Ares/Mars mantles. Children of the Morrigan refer to themselves the children of Badb, Macha, Nemain, Anand or any number of other aspects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:20:14-07:00","id":990018,"title":"","content":"Isn't Mars just the Romanized Ares? They're the same god, overall, are they not? Or am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:29:52-07:00","id":990026,"title":"","content":"The Tuatha write-up for the Morrigan does a good job of showing her as, you know, one very complicated god that has a lot of different faces. By contrast, the Isis/Hathor merger comes across much more as &quot;Hathor doesn't exist. Let's just give Isis the Cows purview and move on.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:32:12-07:00","id":990028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990026#post990026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tuatha write-up for the Morrigan does a good job of showing her as, you know, one very complicated god that has a lot of different faces. By contrast, the Isis/Hathor merger comes across much more as &quot;Hathor doesn't exist. Let's just give Isis the Cows purview and move on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. There are ways to merge gods that gets across the multiple facets and Mantles well. &quot;Isis, also known as Hathor&quot; and then going on to just describe Isis with no Hathor influence is decidedly not the way to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:35:56-07:00","id":990034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990028#post990028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. There are ways to merge gods that gets across the multiple facets and Mantles well. &quot;Isis, also known as Hathor&quot; and then going on to just describe Isis with no Hathor influence is decidedly not the way to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most myths agree That Sekmet became Hathor once she drunk tooo much? Would it be better to throw hathor into the sekmet/bastet mix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:36:57-07:00","id":990035,"title":"","content":"One more voice to the thread. Having read it thoroughly, i see where all going in roughly the same direction. I\u2019m going to write my opini\u00f3n and my main points about the Netjer, but having read all this i\u2019ll write them down more as a way of letting the developers know what i find weird about them than anything else.<br /> <br /> First things first:<br /> <br /> <b>Atamajakki</b>\u2019s point of view fits mine like a glove. Just as she is and says, i\u2019m just an amateur regarding Mythology, but a passionate one when it comes to the Egyptian God and Goddesses.<br /> <br /> At the same time, i\u2019m very aware of the truth spoken by <b>Glamourweaver</b>: this was a religion alive and evolving for more than four thousand years. In that regard, almost everything shifted and changed, and not homogenously. Frequently, the power and position of a God changed with each Nome.<br /> <br /> But, and here i agree with <b>3Comrades</b> completely, these specific parts chosen to portrait the gods of Egypt feel\u2026 wrong in many ways. At least, to me. Is something akin to describing Ares as being an abused child and a shame to the Greeks Gods because Zeus mistreated him as the abusive father he was, or just as Afrodite\u2019s lover. These stances are true, but they are not considered the main description of Ares, God of War.<br /> <br /> And lastly. I\u2019ve loved everything i\u2019ve read about Scion, so far with the exception of this particular Pantheon. For instance, the Tuatha were simply exquisite. (That tiny little bit about pronunciation was a fine delicious detail in particular) I think we have a great game developing in our hands. Let\u2019s give Neall and his team some faith.<br /> <br /> So, my two cents:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>About the feeling of the Pantheon: yes, they are gods of life and it was considered that Egypt \u2013Kemet- was the Blessed Land, something akin to Paradise on Earth, but they themselves should be, as Atamajkki says, relatively grim and stoic. They all follow Ma\u2019at dictates, and there are very few rules more strict than Ma\u2019at\u2019s.</li> </ul><ul><li>About Ma\u2019at, it always seemed to me that she was more a \u201cit\u201d, and definitely atemporal and unconcerned about humans. In a way, it is something akin to the Rule that keeps the universe going. That\u2019s why the gods seem so focused in making the humans respect it. I\u2019m a little disconcerted by the way is treated here as a goddess. I support wholeheartedly the notion of Ma\u2019at as a Titan, or even a more distant entity. Atamajakki\u2019s explanation fits perfectly with what i know about the subject.</li> </ul><ul><li>And about the gods and goddesses: i too woud have liked too some emphasis in their appearance: the symbolism after the animals whose head they carry is essential for these gods.</li> </ul><ul><li>Seth: Seth was the God pof Potency. He is feared, and while in some periods of Egyptian history it was regarded as more destructive and demonic than just any other God in the pantheon, it was never forgotten. Why? Because his tasks were absolutely vital: first he is the God of the Red Sand, and therefore the master of the desert that surrounds Egypt \u2013he is the violent protector of travelers-; second he is the master of storms (something that in all the history of humanity was a really big point by itself)- the vessel and executor of violence-. And last but no least, as Atmajakki says aswell, he is the most commonly-depicted guardian of the solar barge and his eternity-long fight with Apep. I blinked hard when i read about him being \u201cjovial but with a mean streak\u201d. Jovial? That defintely sounded to me the same as calling Ares jovial. And by the way, why does he have a \u201cfriendly competition\u201d with Loki? Seth never was a trickster (in fact, Horus was much more of a trickster than he was \u2013the thingy about lettuce and sperm and all that?-). I don\u2019t understand that at all. [And while the pantheon had historical correlation with others (i could see them having solid ties withthe yazata, and the roman pantheon, for instance) with the Aesir specifically\u2026 i don\u2019t think so. I get perfectly that this is a roleplaying game, not a history class, but well, is just that. It feels weird to me.] Giving him Beasts is something i don\u2019t mind, but maybe change them or add \u201cRed Hyppopothamus\u201d to it.</li> </ul><ul><li>Hathor: I can't think of any reason for Hathor to have not made the list, either. I agree wholeheartedly with all the points Atamajakki raises, most specifically with \u201cI'd sooner see her cut entirely than merged with Isis, a combination I'm not familiar with having ever happened historically\u201d. Special emphasis deserves that \u201cif any merger were to happen it would be with Sekhmet, her fellow solar deity and shared holder of the Eye of Ra title.\u201d</li> </ul><ul><li>I cannot agree with Anubis being passionate, at least in the way it is written here.</li> </ul><ul><li>I would not have a duality between Bast and Sekhmet. As is been said, if Sekhmet merges with any other goddess at all, it should be with Hathor. I won\u2019t repeat or elaborate more on these trio, as what has been written sums perfectly how i feel about it.</li> </ul><ul><li>Isis, to me, was always the loving wife. The wife with esoteric knowledge and master of true names, the wife manipulative enough to cheat when Horus and Seth clashed, fighting for the throne, yes, but loving nonetheless. I don\u2019t have any problema with the notion that Isis would not stand something being or going the way she wanted to, but implying that now despises Osiris is beyond me.</li> </ul><ul><li>Speaking about Osiris\u2026 everything is been said already.</li> </ul><ul><li>I\u2019d want to emphasize this fragment too: \u201cDuat is absolutely full of demons and other perilous threats, to the point where most of all recorded Egyptian religion recorded is advice on how to safely cross through it and protect yourself from its threats. Duat is a dangerous land of magic and monsters with flaming seas and constant challenges for the dead. The text should reflect any of this.\u201d The Book of Going Into the Light \u2013wrongly but usually called The Book of the Dead- is almost purely that: esoteric formulae and words of power the deceased had to know in order to cross the Duat and appease the guardians of the otherwordly lands.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> And by the way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'll give a longer response, but let me clarify one thing - we didn't merge them because of wordcount. I'm sorry I gave that impression. We merged them due to similarity and aspect or because of historical synchretization or trying to look at the gods as singular figures over a period of thousands of years, not because of wordcount. Wordcount is why we chose to put in Ptah instead of Nephthys, for example. Again, sorry about the miscommunication. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This? This is the best answer we could have. I\u2019ve said it already, but once again thank you for the attention and the will to work so openly and thoroughly, Neall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:58:36-07:00","id":990050,"title":"","content":"im interested in seeing how they refocus the next draft and to what degree they'll do so. We might not be privy to it, but it'd be a decent update for backers sometime in the future when the KS is over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:02:54-07:00","id":990055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990003#post990003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI can't imagine it being hard to write her up.<br /> <br /> Nephthys<br /> \u200bCallings: Gaurdian, Leader, Liminal<br /> \u200bPurviews: Beasts (Kite), Death, Health, Sun, Journeys</div> </div> </div> </div>I think her preview should also have something about her role as river goddess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:08:51-07:00","id":990059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990018#post990018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Mars just the Romanized Ares? They're the same god, overall, are they not? Or am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>it's complicate, I believe- while I'm not an expert on religion and mythology, as far as I understand the romans didn't just &quot;stole&quot; the mythology of the greek and gave them different names, but used their very fluid religion system to interpreted their own gods inside the greek myth. Mars especially, as one of the most important deities in the roman religion before that mix and mash, had a well defined personality and role which differed in many ways from Ares, with their roles as war gods being the main reason for the said identification between the two, so while the myths were the same, the greek Ares was quit different from the roman Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:28:11-07:00","id":990069,"title":"","content":"Also- am I the only one who found it strange that the write up spent wordcount on the relationships of the Netjer with the Teotel (which are in the other side of the world) and said nothing about them and the Orisha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:37:31-07:00","id":990072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990069#post990069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also- am I the only one who found it strange that the write up spent wordcount on the relationships of the Netjer with the Teotel (which are in the other side of the world) and said nothing about them and the Orisha?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sahara is a pretty substantial barrier to the mortal cultures associated with the Netjer and Orisha, but it is a little odd that they wouldn't interact. I'm mostly just confused that nothing was made of the Mesopotamian Pantheon (and while I know they aren't in Hero, neither are the Welsh or Nemetendevos but the Tuatha preview mentioned both) and I'm sure the Netjer would like the Shen's orderly ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:37:31-07:00","id":990073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990069#post990069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also- am I the only one who found it strange that the write up spent wordcount on the relationships of the Netjer with the Teotel (which are in the other side of the world) and said nothing about them and the Orisha?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sahara is a pretty substantial barrier to the mortal cultures associated with the Netjer and Orisha, but it is a little odd that they wouldn't interact. I'm mostly just confused that nothing was made of the Mesopotamian Pantheon (and while I know they aren't in Hero, neither are the Welsh or Nemetendevos but the Tuatha preview mentioned both) and I'm sure the Netjer would like the Shen's orderly ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:49:26-07:00","id":990080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990072#post990072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sahara is a pretty substantial barrier to the mortal cultures associated with the Netjer and Orisha, but it is a little odd that they wouldn't interact. I'm mostly just confused that nothing was made of the Mesopotamian Pantheon (and while I know they aren't in Hero, neither are the Welsh or Nemetendevos but the Tuatha preview mentioned both) and I'm sure the Netjer would like the Shen's orderly ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>sure, the Sahara was the explanation I've thought about- but on the other hand, that may have been true few thousands years ago, not in modern times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:15:49-07:00","id":990094,"title":"","content":"Yeah, some things do feel off.<br /> * Bast, Bast, Bast. Almost everything is off. Driven mad, really? The festive protector goddess is too awesome to be turned into a potential Alcoholics Anonymous member.<br /> * Sekhmet/HetHeru can probably work as a single goddess<br /> * Auset and HetHeru should be separate, however. Also, while Auset is manipulative and ambitious, she is painted in such a dark shade of grey here it's almost black. The Apep thing does not work whatsoever. <br /> * Seth - just boring. Which he is not in the original stories. Also, just as an aside, Aesir is plural, singular would be As.<br /> * Either Khnum or Ptah would look better in a future supplement. Too much in common. Would make space for a goddess, maybe.<br /> * Ma'at as a Titan - great idea. Makes less sense as a goddess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:28:41-07:00","id":990098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990094#post990094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Ma'at as a Titan - great idea. Makes less sense as a goddess.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the writeup and what I remember from the Q&amp;A session, would Ma'at make sense as a PRIMORDIAL? Amazing power, too grand and powerful to manifest in the World, and still causes ripples when they manifest in the Overworld? (Forgive my ignorance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:35:46-07:00","id":990101,"title":"","content":"But guys,i've seen Ma'aat as person more than once","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:48:19-07:00","id":990112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990069#post990069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also- am I the only one who found it strange that the write up spent wordcount on the relationships of the Netjer with the Teotel (which are in the other side of the world) and said nothing about them and the Orisha?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought so too, and we know from the lifestyles of Africa pre-colonial times that interactions happened between many peoples of Africa, despite what some may say is a barrier of desert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:13:03-07:00","id":990129,"title":"","content":"Is Helios still the Titan or Primordial of the sun? If so, I would argue that Aten would fit better as an aspect of Helios than an aspect of Re. Lex, you were the original poster. Do you agree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:15:05-07:00","id":990131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990129#post990129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Helios still the Titan or Primordial of the sun? If so, I would argue that Aten would fit better as an aspect of Helios than an aspect of Re. Lex, you were the original poster. Do you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is there only one Titan of each Purview? Because I wouldn't imagine so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:15:05-07:00","id":990132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990129#post990129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Helios still the Titan or Primordial of the sun? If so, I would argue that Aten would fit better as an aspect of Helios than an aspect of Re. Lex, you were the original poster. Do you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is there only one Titan of each Purview? Because I wouldn't imagine so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:16:54-07:00","id":990133,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I have not read the preview yet, but I know a little about Egyptian mythology, and making Aten an aspect of Re just because both are sun deities troubles me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen<br /> &quot;Wildwood Flower&quot; (my theme song)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:06:03-07:00","id":990180,"title":"","content":"Not to labour the point...but Ammut/Ammit is generally described as a <i>Goddess </i>in all my mythology texts, not a male. And Wadjet is the Cobra Goddess of Lower Egypt, and not a title given to a sect of guardians. Hopefully, a lot of these little hiccups will get fixed in the red lines process, because it looks like incomplete work at this point in things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:11:29-07:00","id":990183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990180#post990180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to labour the point...but Ammut/Ammit is generally described as a <i>Goddess </i>in all my mythology texts, not a male. And Wadjet is the Cobra Goddess of Lower Egypt, and not a title given to a sect of guardians. Hopefully, a lot of these little hiccups will get fixed in the red lines process, because it looks like incomplete work at this point in things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how I missed those, but those are pretty basic things to slip up on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:20:21-07:00","id":990187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990180#post990180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to labour the point...but Ammut/Ammit is generally described as a <i>Goddess </i>in all my mythology texts, not a male. And Wadjet is the Cobra Goddess of Lower Egypt, and not a title given to a sect of guardians. Hopefully, a lot of these little hiccups will get fixed in the red lines process, because it looks like incomplete work at this point in things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not incomplete, it's in progress: the first draft, as we explained in the KS. That means the writing gets notated by Neall, and then worked up to his specs by the writer. Some writers work everything out in their first draft and just use the redlines as corrections, and some use the first draft to start a dialogue with the Dev about their big ideas and then fine tune based on that dialogue. From what Neall is saying, this is a case of the latter. It is a process you are getting to see and comment on, and there are many ways writers handle that process which are not wrong, or sloppy, or unprofessional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:37:50-07:00","id":990195,"title":"","content":"I just want to chime in and say I really agree with OP, I think the Netjer in their current state need A LOT of revision back towards the traditional. I'm not opposed to adding extra context and history to their mythology, but here it feels like their entire context has been re-imagined. There is a bit of an alt-universe fanfiction vibe to the current draft, the players are familiar but they all have evil goatees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:43:26-07:00","id":990198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990187#post990187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not incomplete, it's in progress: the first draft, as we explained in the KS. That means the writing gets notated by Neall, and then worked up to his specs by the writer. Some writers work everything out in their first draft and just use the redlines as corrections, and some use the first draft to start a dialogue with the Dev about their big ideas and then fine tune based on that dialogue. From what Neall is saying, this is a case of the latter. It is a process you are getting to see and comment on, and there are many ways writers handle that process which are not wrong, or sloppy, or unprofessional.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for clarifying that. I'll judge the final product not a first draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:51:40-07:00","id":990200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990195#post990195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to chime in and say I really agree with OP, I think the Netjer in their current state need A LOT of revision back towards the traditional. I'm not opposed to adding extra context and history to their mythology, but here it feels like their entire context has been re-imagined. There is a bit of an alt-universe fanfiction vibe to the current draft, the players are familiar but they all have evil goatees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's like those fanfics where it's set in a high school and nobody has powers and they're all humans and also everyone's genders have been switched and so much else has been changed that you're basically writing your own story with the names of characters from another. <br /> <br /> If Anubis is a deeply compassionate individual who resents his role and flees it to help mortals, Sutek killed Osiris on Re's orders, and Osiris is a cruel crimelord of the dead whose conniving wife despises him... that's not Egyptian mythology anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:03:19-07:00","id":990204,"title":"","content":"I personally would have meanted something about Set and Horus' sexual history, I think it would have been interesting.<br /> <br /> I'd add the Passion: Lust to Bast, I know that probably contraversal, but you look at the regilious history of Bubastis, and look at how people see Bast in the public imagination in modern times which given the game is set in modern times and fatebinding, I think it fits, just my person thoughts, not an expert by any means. Also ever seen a cat in heat? Enough said.<br /> <br /> Also controversial I like how the author handled Duat. Nobody with a brain would pick the Netjer with the horrifying afterlife you guys describe, getting to paradise is too unforgiving, and Duat too horrible for those that don't measure up, when another Pantheon, say the Irish Pantheon is generally far more forgiving, they'd just kick the Netjer's ass in worshippers in Modern times, if the Netjer doesn't tone the afterlife punishment down. Same with Greek Pantheon and Hades.<br /> <br /> Most sensible people aren't going to pick a Pantheon on race or Ethnicity over afterlife and other rewards, so this should be taken into concideration.<br /> <br /> I think many of the people focus alittle much on the history and not enough on how an ancient Pantheon adapts to modern times, especially when competing with other major Pantheons and Monotheism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-19-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:15:36-07:00","id":990206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990187#post990187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not incomplete, it's in progress: the first draft, as we explained in the KS. That means the writing gets notated by Neall, and then worked up to his specs by the writer. Some writers work everything out in their first draft and just use the redlines as corrections, and some use the first draft to start a dialogue with the Dev about their big ideas and then fine tune based on that dialogue. From what Neall is saying, this is a case of the latter. It is a process you are getting to see and comment on, and there are many ways writers handle that process which are not wrong, or sloppy, or unprofessional.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I appreciate that, and don't mean to denigrate anyone's capabilities. But if a work is put out for us to read, and we notice so many things that rub us the wrong way, then we, as fans and mythology afficionados, have responsibility to point out what we perceive as errors or omissions. It was in no way meant as an attack on anyone's professionalism. It just seemed to be missing or misinterpreting major aspects of Egyptian mythology in a way the Tuatha and Theoi didn't suffer from. Nothing more or less. I sincerely hope and believe that things will be tidied up, and that we will be happier with the Netjer [and I think the level of support for the project shows that we, the fans, really do want this game, and stand behind OP in their work!], and I look forward to the future version that we may get to see, as well as the other 11 Pantheons waiting in the wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 10-20-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:18:45-07:00","id":990209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990204#post990204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also controversial I like how the author handled Duat. Nobody with a brain would pick the Netjer with the horrifying afterlife you guys describe, getting to paradise is too unforgiving, and Duat too horrible for those that don't measure up, when another Pantheon, say the Irish Pantheon is generally far more forgiving, they'd just kick the Netjer's ass in worshippers in Modern times, if the Netjer doesn't tone the afterlife punishment down. Same with Greek Pantheon and Hades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know, that stark Heaven/Hell contrast hasn't stopped Christianity from being the #1 world religion. If anything it is the threat of consequence in religion that can keep people on the path, especially in Scion where that threat is even more explicitly real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:38:08-07:00","id":990215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990204#post990204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would have meanted something about Set and Horus' sexual history, I think it would have been interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if Scion wants to delve into homosexual incestual rape or not. It seems a touch dark compared to everything else we've seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also controversial I like how the author handled Duat. Nobody with a brain would pick the Netjer with the horrifying afterlife you guys describe, getting to paradise is too unforgiving, and Duat too horrible for those that don't measure up, when another Pantheon, say the Irish Pantheon is generally far more forgiving, they'd just kick the Netjer's ass in worshippers in Modern times, if the Netjer doesn't tone the afterlife punishment down. Same with Greek Pantheon and Hades.<br /> <br /> Most sensible people aren't going to pick a Pantheon on race or Ethnicity over afterlife and other rewards, so this should be taken into concideration. </div> </div> </div>Christianity is still immensely popular and it promises the fires of Hell to people who don't live virtuously. I'm not sure the point you're making stands given that on the table.<br /> <br /> Also, the point of the Egyptian faith is largely to give you the tools to not have to worry about the afterlife; if you live by <i>ma'at</i> then you have nothing to fear from the scale of the heart, and between the funerary spells and being able to call upon Osiris the demons of Duat cannot harm you. (That latter point is why I object so much to Osiris being an extorter of the dead; he's largely there in myth as a bulwark the dead can call upon to keep themselves safe.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-07-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:33:55-07:00","id":990333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=989866#post989866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll give a longer response, but let me clarify one thing - we didn't merge them because of wordcount. I'm sorry I gave that impression. We merged them due to similarity and aspect or because of historical synchretization or trying to look at the gods as singular figures over a period of thousands of years, not because of wordcount. Wordcount is why we chose to put in Ptah instead of Nephthys, for example. Again, sorry about the miscommunication. <br /> <br /> Let me be clear too - I see there's a lot of concern about the Netjer and I share a lot of those concerns. I expect they'll see lots of conversations and redlines coming in the next few weeks and days. I'll probably open develop their second draft for folks so you can see a bit of the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much for jumping into the thread, Neal! And to whoever wrote the chapter - sorry if the response wasn't what you hoped for. We fans are mighty and merciless, but it's just the enthusiasm talking. I'm 100% certain that the final draft is going to be all kinds of Kickass!<br /> <br /> And Neall - your consultative style and (frankly-impressive!) knowledge of the myths has earned a lot of trust - I reckon it's times like this that it'll pay off for you. I, for one, am just going to step back and let you all do your thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:45:05-07:00","id":990343,"title":"","content":"I look forward to the longer response, and hope it happens before the kickstarter ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T04:29:12-07:00","id":990365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989672-dissapointed-by-the-netjer-preview?p=990333#post990333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks so much for jumping into the thread, Neal! And to whoever wrote the chapter - sorry if the response wasn't what you hoped for. We fans are mighty and merciless, but it's just the enthusiasm talking. I'm 100% certain that the final draft is going to be all kinds of Kickass!<br /> <br /> And Neall - your consultative style and (frankly-impressive!) knowledge of the myths has earned a lot of trust - I reckon it's times like this that it'll pay off for you. I, for one, am just going to step back and let you all do your thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second all of this.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think everyone did a good job voicing their concerns as just that: concerns, instead of rabid fan rage. Similarly, Neall and his team have done a great job handling and addressing those concerns.<br /> <br /> \u200bI personally think it's quite telling that this one preview has been the only thing to draw any serious negativity from all of us so far. So far, this team and this project have been batting 1000 and we've had very little to complain about. And even this one complaint is being handled and dealt with reasonably and maturely by all involved. I still remember the early days of the EX3 Kickstarter, and how EVERY update the devs gave was met with a tidal wave of nitpicking and negativity, to the point where they eventually just gave up giving us any updates at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm really glad we've seen nothing like that in this Kickstarter, and I'm also looking forward to just letting the devs do their thing and seeing what they come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}